{"term":"idiom","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:e2ea0beb350d5145b2","definition":"A manner of speaking, a mode of expression peculiar to a language, language family, or group of people.","example":"In English, idiom requires the indefinite article in a phrase such as \"she's an engineer\", whereas in Spanish, idiom forbids it.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["idiomaticness","idiomaticity"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["bromidiom","idiomacy","idiomatic","idiomatical","idiomatically","idiomaticize","idiom blend","idiomless"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/idiom#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2d0cae294509bae7bc","definition":"A language or language variety; specifically, a restricted dialect used in a given historical period, context, etc.","example":"In the idiom of the day, they were sutlers, although today they'd probably be called vendors.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["dialect","language","languoid","lect","vernacular"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["bromidiom","idiomacy","idiomatic","idiomatical","idiomatically","idiomaticize","idiom blend","idiomless"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/idiom#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:03a21523704a481f72","definition":"An established phrasal expression whose meaning may not be deducible from the literal meanings of its component words.","example":"She often spoke in idioms, pining for salad days and complaining about pots calling the kettle black.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["expression","form of words","idiotism","locution","phrase"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["bromidiom","idiomacy","idiomatic","idiomatical","idiomatically","idiomaticize","idiom blend","idiomless"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/idiom#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b1a4b9e3532a8c17f6","definition":"An artistic style (for example, in art, architecture, or music); an instance of such a style.","example":"the idiom of the expressionists","pos":"noun","synonyms":["expression","form of words","idiotism","locution","phrase"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["bromidiom","idiomacy","idiomatic","idiomatical","idiomatically","idiomaticize","idiom blend","idiomless"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/idiom#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/ˈɪdiəm/","uk":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/0/0a/En-uk-idiom.ogg/En-uk-idiom.ogg.mp3","us":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/e/e1/En-us-idiom.ogg/En-us-idiom.ogg.mp3"},"wordFamily":["bromidiom","idiomacy","idiomatic","idiomatical","idiomatically","idiomaticize","idiom blend","idiomless"]}